      "message": "Delete this method. It\u0027s only used once in `validate`, and adds unnecessary redirection.\n\nYou should write something like this in validate():\n\n```\nlicenses \u003d self.extract_license(value)\n\nfor license in licenses:\n    ....\n\nif not allowlist_util.is_a_known_license(license):\n    not_allowlisted.append(license)\n```\n\n---\n\nGenerally, it\u0027s preferable to call `is_a_known_license` inplace. No need to add a redirection via process_license\n\nBonus fix, the current validate() implementation `for license, allowed in licenses:` isn\u0027t idiomatic, as there\u0027s no indication that `licenses` is List[Tuple]. Conventionally, we write: `for thing in things`.",
